### P0: CA Certificate Management

#### CHAP-5v5: Implement CA certificate generation and storage

**Status**: NOT STARTED
**Complexity**: MEDIUM
**Priority**: P0 (CRITICAL - blocks all MITM work)
**Dependencies**: Phase 0.4 (config) complete ✓
**Spec Reference**: PROJECT_SPEC.md lines 66-67 • STATUS-2025-11-30-150747.md lines 325-339
**Beads Issue**: CHAP-5v5

##### Description
Generate self-signed CA certificate and private key on first run, store securely in `~/.config/chaperone/` with appropriate file permissions. This CA will sign all dynamically generated leaf certificates for MITM domains.

##### Implementation Details

**File**: `internal/mitm/ca.go`

Key components:
- `GenerateCA()` - Create RSA 4096-bit private key and self-signed CA certificate
- `LoadCA()` - Load existing CA from filesystem
- `StoreCA()` - Save CA to filesystem with correct permissions
- CA certificate validity: 10 years
- File locations:
  - CA private key: `~/.config/chaperone/ca-key.pem` (permissions 0600)
  - CA certificate: `~/.config/chaperone/ca-cert.pem` (permissions 0644)

**Structure**:
```go
type CA struct {
    cert       *x509.Certificate
    privateKey *rsa.PrivateKey
}

func GenerateCA() (*CA, error)
func LoadCA(keyPath, certPath string) (*CA, error)
func StoreCA(ca *CA, keyPath, certPath string) error
func (ca *CA) SignCertificate(template *x509.Certificate) (*tls.Certificate, error)
```

##### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] CA private key generated with RSA 4096-bit strength
- [ ] CA certificate is valid self-signed certificate
- [ ] CA certificate has 10-year validity period
- [ ] CA certificate has BasicConstraints with CA:TRUE
- [ ] Files stored at `~/.config/chaperone/ca-key.pem` and `ca-cert.pem`
- [ ] CA key file has 0600 permissions (owner read/write only)
- [ ] CA cert file has 0644 permissions (owner read/write, others read)
- [ ] CA loads successfully on subsequent runs (idempotent)
- [ ] CA can sign leaf certificates
- [ ] Unit test verifies CA generation
- [ ] Unit test verifies CA persistence and loading
- [ ] Unit test verifies CA can sign certificates
- [ ] make test passes
- [ ] make test-race passes

##### Technical Notes
- Use `crypto/x509` and `crypto/rsa` from Go standard library
- Set CA certificate Subject: CN="Chaperone Local CA"
- Set KeyUsage: KeyUsageCertSign | KeyUsageCRLSign
- Set ExtKeyUsage: ExtKeyUsageServerAuth
- Use Phase 0.3 logging for CA generation events
- Use Phase 0.2 error types for CA errors
- Create directory `~/.config/chaperone/` if it doesn't exist
- Log CA generation and loading with structured JSON logs

