##### Description
Design and implement Go structs for service configuration and policy definitions. These structures define how services are configured in the TOML config file and how they're represented in memory.

##### Implementation Details

**File**: `internal/service/types.go`

Service configuration structure maps to TOML config:
```toml
[service.openai]
host_pattern = "api.openai.com"
auth_strategy = "bearer"
credential_ref = "env:OPENAI_API_KEY"

[service.openai.policy]
allowed_methods = ["POST", "GET"]
allowed_paths = ["/v1/*"]
max_body_bytes = 2097152
```

**Structure**:
```go
type Service struct {
    Name          string   // e.g., "openai"
    HostPattern   string   // e.g., "api.openai.com"
    AuthStrategy  string   // e.g., "bearer"
    CredentialRef string   // e.g., "env:OPENAI_API_KEY"
    Policy        Policy   // Policy configuration
}

type Policy struct {
    AllowedMethods []string // e.g., ["POST", "GET"]
    AllowedPaths   []string // e.g., ["/v1/*", "/responses/*"]
    MaxBodyBytes   int64    // e.g., 2097152 (2MB)
    ClientGroups   []string // e.g., ["devtools"] (future)
}

func (s *Service) Validate() error
func (p *Policy) Validate() error
```

##### Acceptance Criteria
