##### Description
Establish standard TLS connection to upstream API server with proper certificate validation using system trust store. This is the outbound leg of the MITM proxy - client TLS terminates at Chaperone, upstream TLS is standard client connection.

##### Implementation Details

**File**: `internal/client/client.go` (new package)

Outbound HTTPS client design:
- Use system certificate pool (not Chaperone CA)
- Standard TLS handshake with upstream
- Connection pooling for performance
- Proper timeout configuration
- Respect HTTP_PROXY environment variable (enterprise proxy support)
- NEVER set InsecureSkipVerify

**Structure**:
```go
type Client struct {
    httpClient *http.Client
    logger     *slog.Logger
}

func NewClient(logger *slog.Logger) *Client
func (c *Client) Do(req *http.Request) (*http.Response, error)
```

##### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] TLS connection to upstream succeeds with valid certificate
- [ ] Certificate validation uses system trust store
- [ ] Expired/invalid upstream certificates rejected (connection fails)
- [ ] Connection pooling enabled (MaxIdleConnsPerHost: 100)
- [ ] Timeouts enforced (30s connect, 60s read/write)
- [ ] HTTP/2 support enabled (automatic with Go http.Client)
- [ ] HTTP_PROXY environment variable respected (for enterprise proxies)
- [ ] Connection establishment logged
- [ ] Unit test with mock upstream server
- [ ] Integration test with real API (google.com)
- [ ] make test passes
- [ ] make test-race passes

##### Technical Notes
- Use `http.DefaultTransport` as base, customize timeouts
- Use `tls.Config` with system cert pool: `x509.SystemCertPool()`
- Set `DialContext` timeout: 30 seconds
- Set `TLSHandshakeTimeout`: 10 seconds
- Set `ResponseHeaderTimeout`: 60 seconds
- Log connection errors clearly (cert validation, timeout, network)
- Use Phase 0.3 logging for client events
- This client is used for ALL upstream connections (MITM and future auth flows)

