### P1: Policy Enforcement (Basic)

#### CHAP-c2s: Implement path and method policy enforcement

**Status**: NOT STARTED
**Complexity**: MEDIUM
**Priority**: P1 (HIGH - required for security)
**Dependencies**: CHAP-a1z (service registry), CHAP-90r (HTTP handler)
**Spec Reference**: PROJECT_SPEC.md lines 166-179 • STATUS-2025-11-30-150747.md lines 486-490
**Beads Issue**: CHAP-c2s

##### Description
Implement policy enforcement for allowed paths and methods, returning 403 Forbidden for violations. This provides basic security by restricting which paths and HTTP methods can be proxied for each service.

##### Implementation Details

**File**: `internal/service/policy.go`

Policy enforcement flow:
1. After reading HTTP request, before forwarding to upstream
2. Get service from registry
3. Check if request method in AllowedMethods (if configured)
4. Check if request path matches AllowedPaths glob patterns (if configured)
5. Check if request body size <= MaxBodyBytes (if configured)
6. If any check fails, return 403 Forbidden with clear error message
7. If all checks pass, continue to upstream forwarding

**Structure**:
```go
type PolicyEnforcer struct {
    logger *slog.Logger
}

func NewPolicyEnforcer(logger *slog.Logger) *PolicyEnforcer
func (e *PolicyEnforcer) EnforcePolicy(req *http.Request, policy Policy) error
func (e *PolicyEnforcer) checkMethod(method string, allowedMethods []string) bool
func (e *PolicyEnforcer) checkPath(path string, allowedPaths []string) bool
func (e *PolicyEnforcer) checkBodySize(contentLength int64, maxBytes int64) bool
```

##### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Allowed methods enforced (POST, GET, etc.)
- [ ] Disallowed methods return 403 Forbidden
- [ ] Allowed paths enforced with glob matching (/v1/\* matches /v1/chat)
- [ ] Disallowed paths return 403 Forbidden
- [ ] Body size limit enforced (Content-Length check)
- [ ] Oversized bodies return 413 Payload Too Large
- [ ] Empty allowlists allow all (if AllowedMethods=[], allow all methods)
- [ ] Policy violations logged with details (method, path, size)
- [ ] Unit test verifies method enforcement
- [ ] Unit test verifies path glob matching
- [ ] Unit test verifies body size enforcement
- [ ] Unit test verifies empty allowlist behavior
- [ ] Integration test verifies 403 responses
- [ ] make test passes

##### Technical Notes
- Use glob matching for paths (implement simple glob: `/v1/*` matches `/v1/anything`)
- Match exact paths if no wildcard: `/v1/chat` matches only `/v1/chat`
- Case-sensitive path matching (HTTP paths are case-sensitive)
- Check Content-Length header for body size (before reading body)
- Return clear error messages: "method POST not allowed", "path /admin not allowed"
- Use Phase 0.2 error types for policy violations
- Log policy violations with request ID

