## Testing Strategy

### Unit Tests (per component)

**CA Management** (`internal/mitm/ca_test.go`):
- CA generation with correct key size and validity
- CA persistence and loading
- CA signing of leaf certificates

**Certificate Generation** (`internal/mitm/cert_test.go`):
- Leaf certificate generation for hostname
- Certificate caching (hit/miss)
- Certificate expiration and regeneration
- SAN correctness

**Service Registry** (`internal/service/registry_test.go`):
- Service registration and lookup
- Case-insensitive matching
- Port stripping
- Concurrent access (with -race)

**Domain Matching** (`internal/service/matcher_test.go`):
- Configured domain returns true
- Non-configured domain returns false
- Case and port handling

**TLS Handshake** (`internal/proxy/tunnel_test.go`):
- MITM mode with mock TLS connection
- Transparent tunnel mode (existing Phase 1 tests)
- Domain routing logic

**Outbound Client** (`internal/client/client_test.go`):
- TLS connection to mock upstream
- Certificate validation
- Timeout enforcement

**HTTP Proxying** (`internal/proxy/mitm_handler_test.go`):
- Request parsing and forwarding
- Response streaming
- Header preservation
- Error handling

**Policy Enforcement** (`internal/service/policy_test.go`):
- Method allowlist
- Path glob matching
- Body size limits

### Integration Tests

**MITM Flow** (`test/integration/mitm_test.go`):
- Complete MITM flow with trusted CA
- Selective MITM vs transparent tunnel
- Certificate trust validation
- Policy enforcement end-to-end

### Manual Tests

After Phase 2 completion, these manual tests should work:

```bash
# Test 1: Initialize and start server
./chaperone init openai
./chaperone run --config chaperone.toml
# Expected: CA generated, services loaded, server starts

# Test 2: Trust CA certificate
# macOS:
sudo security add-trusted-cert -d -r trustRoot -k /Library/Keychains/System.keychain ~/.config/chaperone/ca-cert.pem
# Linux:
sudo cp ~/.config/chaperone/ca-cert.pem /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/chaperone-ca.crt
sudo update-ca-certificates

# Test 3: MITM for configured domain
export HTTPS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:4010
curl -v https://api.openai.com/v1/models
# Expected: MITM occurs, request decrypted (NO auth yet, will get 401)

# Test 4: Transparent tunnel for non-configured domain
curl -v https://www.google.com
# Expected: Transparent tunnel, no MITM

# Test 5: Policy enforcement
curl -X DELETE https://api.openai.com/v1/models
# Expected: 403 Forbidden (DELETE not allowed)

curl https://api.openai.com/admin/secret
# Expected: 403 Forbidden (path not allowed)
```

